    <briefdescription>
<para>Type-safe wrapper for move operations with automatic validation. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Provides a zero-cost abstraction over move operations with safety guarantees:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Pre-move validation</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Post-move source cleanup</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Move destination validation</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Compile-time move type checking</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Type being safely moved</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Example: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">std::vector&lt;int&gt;<sp/>data<sp/>=<sp/>{1,<sp/>2,<sp/>3};</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>safe<sp/>=<sp/>SafeMove&lt;std::vector&lt;int&gt;&gt;<ref refid="classthemis_1_1security_1_1_safe_move_1a07caa1af4b8fa3258bbe79f0666ee23c" kindref="member">::create</ref>(std::move(data));</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="keyword">auto</highlight><highlight class="normal"><sp/>result<sp/>=<sp/>safe.take();<sp/></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Takes<sp/>ownership,<sp/>validates<sp/>state</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
